Quietly noting that identical pixels rarely need repeating, here's a compact approach: compute a strong hash for the incoming bytes, use it as a dedupe key, and persist the thumbnail only when that hash isn't already cached. Below is a ready-to-drop implementation — with a small concurrent map for tracking hashes and a cache directory under the user's home. If you prefer streaming to disk instead of buffering fully in memory (for very large thumbnails), I can adjust it.

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentMap;

public class ThumbCacheHelper {
    // simple in-memory index of hash -> cached file path
    private static final ConcurrentMap<String, Path> THUMB_HASH_MAP = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final Path THUMB_CACHE_DIR = Paths.get(System.getProperty("user.home"), ".thumbcache");

    /**
     * Caches the received thumbnail image.
     * @param fileInfo the information about the file
     * @param inputStream the input stream containing the thumbnail image data
     * @throws IOException if an I/O error occurs
     */
    public static void cacheReceiveThumb(BaseFileInfo fileInfo, InputStream inputStream) throws IOException {
        if (fileInfo == null || inputStream == null) {
            return;
        }

        // Read all bytes from input stream (small thumbnails assumed). Close stream after use.
        final byte[] data;
        try (ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream()) {
            byte[] buffer = new byte[8192];
            int read;
            while ((read = inputStream.read(buffer)) != -1) {
                baos.write(buffer, 0, read);
            }
            data = baos.toByteArray();
        } finally {
            try { inputStream.close(); } catch (IOException ignored) {}
        }

        if (data.length == 0) {
            return;
        }

        // Compute a strong hash (SHA-256) to detect duplicates
        final String hash;
        try {
            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
            byte[] digest = md.digest(data);
            hash = bytesToHex(digest);
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            // Unlikely, but wrap into IOException to conform to method signature
            throw new IOException("Hash algorithm not available", e);
        }

        // Ensure cache directory exists
        Files.createDirectories(THUMB_CACHE_DIR);

        // Determine extension from original filename if possible (fall back to .thumb)
        String ext = extractExtension(fileInfo);
        if (ext == null) ext = ".thumb";

        Path target = THUMB_CACHE_DIR.resolve(hash + ext);

        // Prevent race conditions: synchronize on interned hash string
        synchronized (hash.intern()) {
            if (Files.exists(target)) {
                // Already stored; update in-memory map to point to existing file
                THUMB_HASH_MAP.putIfAbsent(hash, target);
                return;
            }

            // If another thread inserted the mapping while we waited, respect it
            Path existing = THUMB_HASH_MAP.get(hash);
            if (existing != null && Files.exists(existing)) {
                return;
            }

            // Write file atomically (CREATE_NEW to avoid accidental overwrite)
            try {
                Files.write(target, data, StandardOpenOption.CREATE_NEW);
                THUMB_HASH_MAP.put(hash, target);
            } catch (FileAlreadyExistsException faee) {
                // Another thread/process created it; ensure map points to it
                THUMB_HASH_MAP.putIfAbsent(hash, target);
            }
        }
    }

    // Helpers

    private static String extractExtension(BaseFileInfo fileInfo) {
        try {
            // Assume BaseFileInfo has getName(); if not, callers can adapt this helper.
            String name = fileInfo.getName();
            if (name != null) {
                int idx = name.lastIndexOf('.');
                if (idx >= 0 && idx < name.length() - 1) {
                    return name.substring(idx);
                }
            }
        } catch (Throwable ignored) {
            // If BaseFileInfo doesn't expose name, fall back to null -> use default extension.
        }
        return null;
    }

    private static String bytesToHex(byte[] bytes) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(bytes.length * 2);
        for (byte b : bytes) {
            sb.append(Character.forDigit((b >> 4) & 0xF, 16));
            sb.append(Character.forDigit((b & 0xF), 16));
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```

A couple of soft notes:
- This buffers the whole thumbnail in memory; if you expect much larger streams, we can switch to streaming to a temporary file and hashing on-the-fly to avoid large allocations.
- Hash collisions are extremely unlikely with SHA-256; if absolute certainty is required, a byte-by-byte compare of candidate files could be added when a hash match is found.
