- uniform_int_distribution guarantees each integer in [0,19] is equally likely (no modulo bias).
- If you want reproducible runs (e.g., testing), replace rd() with a fixed seed: std::mt19937 gen(12345);
- For many draws, keep the generator (gen) outside any loop so you don’t re-seed each time.
- If you need cryptographic-grade randomness, std::random_device may not be sufficient on all platforms — consider platform-specific crypto APIs or libs.

